# nr-office-formula-lib-financial: reduced by the wire audit (t19). Applied: the TABLES registration, the UTF-16 Value integration, the shared pow / add / mul helpers, the fixture index entry office-financial.

## Gate before native office.run is enabled (lead; containment)
mixdog_xlsx_formula is called only through mixdog-ooxml today and office.run is not in mixdog-exthost-worker native_methods (main_entry.rs lists only document, image, media, office.sweepJournals, ooxml.text, pdf.* names). A formula can be non-terminating (IRR(cashflows, +Infinity) does not end; a raw +Infinity CUM end period likewise). Native Office recalculation MUST run inside the owned ext-worker process with the blocking registry path (register_blocking) and the pool cancellation retained (mixdog-exthost pool.rs CANCEL_GRACE 5 s then stop(io) / io.kill.kill()); never on a daemon task or spawn_blocking thread, which this pool boundary cannot kill. Before enabling office.run, cancel the actual IRR(+Infinity) case in an isolated child and verify its PID is gone after the grace (do not run it in a unit-test or daemon process). The existing pool regression a_parser_that_ignores_the_cancel_is_ended_after_the_grace covers the mechanism, not the future handler. No cooperative cancellation API or new limit may replace the process boundary without approval.
